From f235f6dc9cd9fd5bed79c3acc36e6bdd56856cbf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <dev@infoverify.local>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 09:03:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add BVN Modification: 8-type manual-review flow + BVN/NIN
 match-check helper

Backend (mirrors nin-modification.service.ts's manual-review pattern -
Techhub has no live BVN Modification API either):
- New BVN_MODIFICATION TransactionType + migration.
- bvn-modification.service.ts: 8 types (update_name, update_phone,
  update_dob, update_address, and the four combined variants), each with
  its own field config matching the reference screenshots - every type
  also carries BVN Number, NIN Number, and Enrollment Type
  (Agency/Bank + a conditional bank_name select, list per the user's
  spec, BOA BANK deduped). submitBvnModificationRequest() debits the
  wallet, renders a submission-record PDF, and leaves the transaction
  PENDING for manual admin processing, same as NIN Modification.
- checkBvnNinMatch(): the 'not sure how many things need fixing' helper.
  Runs a REAL BVN slip + NIN slip purchase (each wallet-debited at its
  normal price, reusing purchaseBvnSlip/purchaseNinByNin as-is) and
  compares name + DOB between the two (tolerant of several Techhub field
  -name spellings), returning which of the four single/combo name+DOB
  types is suggested.
- bvn-modification.routes.ts: /types, /prices, /banks, /history, one
  /:type/submit route per type, and /match-check. A superRefine enforces
  the one cross-field rule the generic per-field schema can't express -
  bank_name required+valid iff enrollment_type is BANK, blank otherwise.
- Admin: completeBvnModification/downloadBvnModificationPdf actions on
  the Transaction resource (mirrors completeBvnLicense's pattern
  exactly), reverse()'s PENDING allowlist extended, and a SUPER_ADMIN
  -only audited PDF route (admin/bvn-modification.ts, mirrors
  admin/nin-modification.ts).

Frontend:
- BvnModificationPage.tsx at /bvn-modification (services.ts flipped to
  implemented: true): asks up front whether the customer needs one fix
  or two combined, or is unsure; 'unsure' runs the match-check above and
  suggests a type before handing off to the same dynamic field-config
  form NIN Modification already uses (extended with a 'bvn' input kind
  and the enrollment/bank conditional field).
- BvnModificationConsent.tsx: same consent-gate pattern as
  ModificationConsent.tsx, reworded for BVN/banks/NIBSS instead of NIN/
  NIMC.

Note: could not run a full backend tsc/prisma generate in this sandbox -
network egress here blocks binaries.prisma.sh, which prisma generate
needs (this affects the whole repo, not just these files - even a clean
clone fails the same way here). Frontend tsc + vite build both pass
clean. Backend code was hand-verified against nin-modification.service
.ts/.routes.ts's working shape and brace/paren-balance checked.
